  "segments": [
   {
    "id": "t1",
    "start": 0.0,
    "end": 5.84,
    "text": "Canola oil is toxic. Here's how it's made. It starts with the seeds of a raped plant,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t2",
    "start": 5.84,
    "end": 10.56,
    "text": "which are completely toxic to humans. In order to make canola oil, these plants must be specially"
   },
   {
    "id": "t3",
    "start": 10.56,
    "end": 17.04,
    "text": "bred to lower the levels of erusic acid, a toxic fatty acid strongly associated with heart lesions."
   },
   {
    "id": "t4",
    "start": 17.04,
    "end": 21.28,
    "text": "These seeds are then ground at high temperatures to extract the fragile oil,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t5",
    "start": 21.28,
    "end": 26.4,
    "text": "which is inevitably oxidized because of this harsh process. This oil must then be washed"
   },
   {
    "id": "t6",
    "start": 26.4,
    "end": 30.32,
    "text": "with solvents like hexane, a known neurological toxin."
   },
   {
    "id": "t7",
    "start": 30.32,
    "end": 35.04,
    "text": "Then it must be processed with bleaching and deodorization so it doesn't smell rancid like it"
   },
   {
    "id": "t8",
    "start": 35.04,
    "end": 40.72,
    "text": "really is. After all of these steps, the canola oil is left oxidized, contaminated with solvents,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t9",
    "start": 40.72,
    "end": 47.6,
    "text": "and containing significant levels of trans fatty acids. And this oil is marketed to you as healthy"
   },
   {
    "id": "t10",
    "start": 47.6,
    "end": 52.8,
    "text": "by the American Heart Association and found in so many of our food stuffs today. If you want to"
   },
   {
    "id": "t11",
    "start": 52.8,
    "end": 56.3,
    "text": "If you want to be healthy, get this damaged oil out of your diet completely."
   }
  ]
 },
